  "notes": "Source: official Sacred Heart University Registrar major checksheet 'BS in Computer Science (Fall 2024 & Later)', effective Fall 2024, which prints a suggested four-year sequence of study (transcribed term-by-term below). Requirements cross-checked against the official 2024-2025 Undergraduate Catalog Computer Science Major page (https://sacredheart.smartcatalogiq.com/en/2024-2025/2024-2025-undergraduate-catalog/jack-welch-college-of-business/school-of-computing/computer-science-and-engineering/computer-science-major/). Transcription method: PDF downloaded from sacredheart.edu 2026-09-30 and text-extracted with pdftotext -layout, then manually mapped to schema. CAVEATS: (1) The sheet's Year 3 Semester 6 line prints 'CS 461 Software Engineering'; the same sheet's required curriculum and the 2024-2025 catalog list Software Engineering as CS 312 (3 cr), and CS 461 exists only as a discontinued 2020-curriculum elective code - transcribed as CS 312. (2) The sequence prints 'PY111/113 General Physics I and Lab' and 'PY 112/114 General Physics II and Lab'; the same sheet's supporting-courses list shows PY151/153 and the catalog lists PY 151/PY 153 and PY 152/PY 154 - transcribed as PY 151/153 and PY 152/154. (3) CREDIT TOTAL: the sheet states a 120-credit degree minimum but the transcribed 8-term sequence sums to 119 credits; the checksheet side lists a 1-credit free elective that is not placed in any term of the printed sequence, which accounts for the gap. total_credits uses the sequence's own sum (119) per the sequence-total rule. (4) The sequence labels all four elective slots 'CS Elec'; the requirement side splits them into two CS electives (CS 421/CS 432/CS 481/CS 482 per sheet; catalog renames CS 432 to CS 332 'Cloud Computing') and two SCSE electives (ITI 350/ITI 338/CY 367/GDD 271/ENGR 212) - modeled as two CS-elective choice slots (Fall Year 4) and two SCSE-elective choice slots (Spring Year 4). (5) CORE/LAE slots are student-choice placeholders; titles/descriptions only, not catalog courses. (6) CS 390 Internship is listed on the sheet as 'Summer or Fall'; placed in Fall Year 3 per the printed sequence. (7) Prereqs transcribed only where stated in official catalog course descriptions (CS 112<-CS 111; CS 215/CS 241/CS 311/CS 339<-CS 112; CS 341<-CS 241; MA 152<-MA 151; MA 261<-MA 152; PY 152/154<-PY 151/153). MA 151 has a placement/MA-140 entry path per catalog - details not modeled.",
